^{2}{x}_{1}+t{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-{t}^{2}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -{t}^{2} & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304851 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304229 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304851 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304365 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304851 1069 "q-330769" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304851 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304851 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+y,\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) Method. Complete the first row of the table below, given that the step size is $Δx=1.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $2$ | $4$ | $5$ | $9$ | {{field-1}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(1)≈$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304851 1072 #uuid "5f6b41d2-317f-53ff-8317-f17fed8f2b61" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304851 1074 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c\n$$\n\nthe increment in $y$ using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method with step size $Δx$ is computed as the weighted average of four sample slopes:\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the initial point $(x,y),