edicted slope at this point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =2\\cdot {x}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{p} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\frac{5}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ |\n\nThe value of $x$ in the next row is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ To get the value of $y$ in the next row, we add $Δy$ to $y:$\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy=1+\\frac{7}{8}=\\frac{15}{8}.\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{15}{8}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈\\frac{15}{8}.$" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304879 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304418 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304879 1069 "q-331017" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304879 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186304879 1071 "Given that $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ for $s>0$, find $L{u(t-6)({t}^{2}-t+3)},$ where $u(t)$ is the unit step function." 13194139533414 1