l initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{2t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305039 1072 #uuid "43b7f8d9-cde0-5a9e-bbd2-55f66df84429" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305039 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{s+1}} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-1\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{4}{s-2}} \\\\  & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1\\cdot t}+4{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}+4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{-t}+4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304109 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304512 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304710 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304751 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1069 "q-332391" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{2t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1072 #uuid "8583693b-a733-5fca-ba20-8078cfaf6308" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305040 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305041 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304123 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305041 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304379 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305041 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304594 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305041 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304728 13194139533414 17592186045585 true