t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}} \\\\  & =5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ 5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305044 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304390 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305044 1069 "q-33249" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305044 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305044 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through $P(3,-5,7)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨3,6,9⟩.$" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305044 1072 #uuid "f41292b0-6019-55a6-adaa-1776104a9250" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305044 1074 "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y-(-5)}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y+5}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}.\n$$" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [1759218630504