aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/f1/f1335e5420fe6e475cded1092e9b1ba621e0d88f46110b69ffef5e35ed080d6e.png)\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=2x\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/a5/a53bb4e6cd7552b92424b168d0cda90fa1085b5e72fbf8a3c37a3a948bdcf9ad.png)\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/92/923e79b665f4529e579776188731896e6ce301743394e2102132f2cee7f6eaa9.png)" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305133 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304457 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305133 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304467 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305133 1069 "q-332836" 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305133 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533414 17592186045585 true] [17592186305133 1071 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8y=10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=A{e}^{2x}\\,+\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$